# Byte-for-byte parity IS the product: manifests, sidecars and golden vectors commit to
# the SHA-256 of file *bytes*, so a checkout that rewrites line endings changes the very
# thing the protocol pins. With core.autocrlf=true and no .gitattributes, a fresh clone on
# Windows fails the Wycheproof corpus integrity gate outright: the bytes it hashes are
# not the bytes that were committed. Normalizing to LF makes the working tree identical on
# every platform.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never touched: any translation here corrupts the artifact.
*.zip binary
*.bin binary
*.pdf binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
